dulum swings  with the times it was a story to be  understood maybe asking too much of a  public that wants to kill the messenger  brings the bad news but it behooves us  to let the chips fall where they may  and above all to be fair engraved in the  mantle in the State Dining Room at the  White House below a magnificent portrait  of Lincoln is a prayer by John Adams  which says may only good and wise men  live here and surely we all hope for  that and Lincoln said let the people  know the facts in the country will be  safe I believe that and I believe that  we should keep an eye on presidents who  have life-and-death power over all  humanity today to keep the people  informed and democracy alive thank you  ladies and gentlemen thank you very much  ladies and gentlemen thank you very much  Helen I hope that you will give us the  chance to get your text I would like to  arrange somewhere to have it reprinted  not for what you advice you gave for  presidents so much as for the advice you  gave to reporters I don't think that any  of us in this room intend to be  President but what you said about what  we need to do needs to be reviewed over  and over again by us thank you very much  thank you ladies and gentlemen  that was Brian Berger  please take inspector  you want to tell them that confession  yeah

